DestroyFunc TileAutoMappedDo
AddToFunc   TileAutoMappedDo
+ I ThisWindow (Transient) Break
+ I ThisWindow (!Maximizable) Break
+ I ThisWindow (State 1) Break
+ I ThisWindow (State 2) Break
+ I ThisWindow (Iconic) Break
+ I ThisWindow ("florence") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("Florence") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("florence-sticky") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("Florence-sticky") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("FvwmPager") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("FvwmButtons") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("Conky") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("Conky*") Break
+ I PipeRead `fvwm-tile mapped $[w.id] $[w.screen] $[w.desk] $[w.pagex] $[w.pagey] $[monitor.$[w.screen].width] $[monitor.$[w.screen].height] $[pointer.screen] $[monitor.$[pointer.screen].desk] $[monitor.$[pointer.screen].pagex] $[monitor.$[pointer.screen].pagey] $[monitor.$[pointer.screen].width] $[monitor.$[pointer.screen].height] $[monitor.primary] $[taskbar_h] $[monitor.$[w.screen].x] $[monitor.$[w.screen].y] $[vp.width] $[vp.height] $[monitor.$[pointer.screen].x] $[monitor.$[pointer.screen].y]`

DestroyFunc TileDestroyed
AddToFunc   TileDestroyed
+ I PipeRead `fvwm-tile drop $[w.id]`

DestroyFunc TileRestore
AddToFunc   TileRestore
+ I SuperChord
+ I PipeRead `fvwm-tile remove $[w.id]`
+ I ThisWindow (Maximized) Maximize False
+ I State 3 False
+ I DestroyWindowStyle
+ I Raise
+ I Focus

# Super+Tab: immediate focus cycle on this monitor + pager page (tile or
# float).  Not the Alt+Tab WindowList.  Super+Shift+Tab walks backward.
# Skip pager/taskbar/Florence/Conky via CirculateSkip + WindowListSkip.
DestroyFunc SuperTabSelect
AddToFunc   SuperTabSelect
+ I WindowShade False
+ I Iconify off
+ I Raise
+ I Focus NoWarp

DestroyFunc SuperTab
AddToFunc   SuperTab
+ I SuperChord
+ I Next (CurrentPage, CurrentScreen, AcceptsFocus, !Iconic, \
	!CirculateSkip, !WindowListSkip) SuperTabSelect

DestroyFunc SuperTabBack
AddToFunc   SuperTabBack
+ I SuperChord
+ I Prev (CurrentPage, CurrentScreen, AcceptsFocus, !Iconic, \
	!CirculateSkip, !WindowListSkip) SuperTabSelect

# Super+`: same cycle, but only WM_CLASS of the focused window.
# Bind like SuperTab (no Current on the Key line; Current there skips
# CirculateSkip focus and the chord never runs).  Current wraps PipeRead
# so $[w.class] expands from the focused window.
DestroyFunc SuperGrave
AddToFunc   SuperGrave
+ I SuperChord
+ I Current PipeRead `bvwm-same-class Next $[w.class]`

DestroyFunc SuperGraveBack
AddToFunc   SuperGraveBack
+ I SuperChord
+ I Current PipeRead `bvwm-same-class Prev $[w.class]`

# Super+Shift+comma / Super+Shift+period: dwm tagmon. Send the focused
# window to the previous or next output (top to bottom, then left to
# right, wrapping). A fullscreen window is sized to that output.
# One output does nothing. The old auto-tile cell reflows. An auto-tile
# cell on the destination takes the window. A manual tile keeps its
# fractions of the destination (half of eDP-1 stays half of DP-4). A
# maximized window is maximized there. A window that leaves an auto-tile
# cell for a monitor that is not auto-tiled becomes a normal floating
# window at that output's top-left. A send shows tile-prev or tile-next.
# Staying on one output does not. SuperChord runs first so releasing
# Shift and then Super does not open the start menu.
DestroyFunc TileSendMon
AddToFunc   TileSendMon
+ I SuperChord
+ I ThisWindow (Transient) Break
+ I ThisWindow (CirculateSkip) Break
+ I ThisWindow (!Maximizable) Break
+ I ThisWindow (WindowListSkip) Break
+ I ThisWindow ("florence") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("Florence") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("FvwmPager") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("FvwmButtons") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("Conky") Break
+ I ThisWindow ("Conky*") Break
+ I ThisWindow (EWMHFullscreen) InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_fs 1
+ I TestRc (NoMatch) InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_fs 0
+ I ThisWindow (State 3) InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_st 1
+ I TestRc (NoMatch) InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_st 0
+ I ThisWindow (Maximized) InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_max 1
+ I TestRc (NoMatch) InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_max 0
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_from $[w.screen]
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_sw $[monitor.$[w.screen].width]
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_sh $[monitor.$[w.screen].height]
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_sx $[monitor.$[w.screen].x]
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_sy $[monitor.$[w.screen].y]
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_ww $[w.width]
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_wh $[w.height]
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_wx $[w.x]
+ I InfoStoreAdd bvwm_tile_wy $[w.y]
+ I MoveToScreen $0
+ I PipeRead `fvwm-tile send $[infostore.bvwm_tile_from] $[w.screen] $[w.id] $[monitor.$[w.screen].desk] $[monitor.$[w.screen].pagex] $[monitor.$[w.screen].pagey] $[monitor.$[w.screen].width] $[monitor.$[w.screen].height] $[monitor.primary] $[taskbar_h] $[monitor.$[w.screen].x] $[monitor.$[w.screen].y] $[vp.width] $[vp.height] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_fs] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_st] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_max] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_sw] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_sh] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_sx] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_sy] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_ww] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_wh] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_wx] $[infostore.bvwm_tile_wy] $0`

# Close is the Alt+F4 action. A bare Close here asks for a click:
# the key has no window. Current names the focus.
# CirculateSkip keeps the pager and the taskbar. SuperChord runs
# first so release does not open the menu.
DestroyFunc TileClose
AddToFunc   TileClose
+ I SuperChord
+ I Current (CirculateSkip) Break
+ I Current Close

# Super+Enter opens fvwm-xterm. SuperChord runs first so releasing
# Super does not open the start menu.
DestroyFunc BvwmXTerm
AddToFunc   BvwmXTerm
+ I SuperChord
+ I Exec exec fvwm-xterm

# Super+Left/Right: halves. Super+Up: fill working area (covers pager).
# Super+Down: restore floating (also drops the window from Super+T layout).
# Super+Shift+Up/Down: top/bottom halves. Super+Shift+Left/Right: top quarters.
# Super+Ctrl+Left/Right: bottom quarters.
# Super+Ctrl+Up: insert into layout, or rotate/swap the focused window.
# Super+Ctrl+Down: previous cell (floating), or eject (auto-tile).
# Super+Tab / Super+Shift+Tab: cycle focus (no WindowList).
# Super+` / Super+Shift+`: same, limited to the focused window's class.
# Super+W: close the focused window (Alt+F4). A tile has no close
# button, and F4 is behind Fn when Fn-lock is on.
# Super+Enter: the Start-menu terminal. SuperChord runs first so
# release does not open the menu.
Key Left	A 4	Current TileApply 50 100 0 0
Key Right	A 4	Current TileApply 50 100 50 0
Key Up		A 4	Current TileMaximize
Key Down	A 4	Current TileRestore
Key Up		A 4S	Current TileApply 100 50 0 0
Key Down	A 4S	Current TileApply 100 50 0 50
Key Left	A 4S	Current TileApply 50 50 0 0
Key Right	A 4S	Current TileApply 50 50 50 0
Key Left	A 4C	Current TileApply 50 50 0 50
Key Right	A 4C	Current TileApply 50 50 50 50
Key Up		A 4C	Current TileInsert
Key Down	A 4C	Current TileRotateBack
Key t		A 4	TileAutoToggle
Key T		A 4	TileAutoToggle
Key w		A 4	TileClose
Key W		A 4	TileClose
Key Return	A 4	BvwmXTerm
Key comma	A MS	-
Key period	A MS	-
Key comma	A 4S	Current TileSendMon prev
Key period	A 4S	Current TileSendMon next
Key Tab		A 4	SuperTab
Key Tab		A 4S	SuperTabBack
Key ISO_Left_Tab	A 4	SuperTabBack
Key ISO_Left_Tab	A 4S	SuperTabBack
Key grave		A 4	SuperGrave
Key grave		A 4S	SuperGraveBack
Key quoteleft		A 4	SuperGrave
Key quoteleft		A 4S	SuperGraveBack
Key dead_grave		A 4	SuperGrave
Key dead_grave		A 4S	SuperGraveBack
Key asciitilde		A 4	SuperGraveBack
Key asciitilde		A 4S	SuperGraveBack
Key dead_tilde		A 4	SuperGraveBack
Key dead_tilde		A 4S	SuperGraveBack

# New windows join the auto-tile layout. Closed windows leave it.
# A second FvwmEvent alias, so the stock desk event module stays.
DestroyModuleConfig FvwmEventTile: *
*FvwmEventTile: add_window TileAutoMapped
*FvwmEventTile: destroy_window TileDestroyed
KillModule FvwmEventTile
Module FvwmEvent FvwmEventTile
